diff --git a/Documentation/mm/hbf-control-plane.rst b/Documentation/mm/hbf-control-plane.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9f849e6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/mm/hbf-control-plane.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+HBF-Like Memory Tier Control Plane
+==================================
+
+This document describes an experimental RFC control plane for HBF-like warm
+memory tiers exposed through CXL Type-3 memory, DAX mappings, or memory
+hotplugged capacity.
+
+The target model is not a standalone block device subsystem. The target model is
+an mm-facing hint path for byte-addressable or migration-managed warm capacity
+that sits below HBM and above cold storage.
+
+Goals
+-----
+
+- Treat HBF-like capacity as a warm memory tier.
+- Keep the first RFC close to ``Documentation/mm/`` and ``mm/``.
+- Allow an RFC frontend such as ``/dev/hbfctl`` only as a temporary ingestion
+  surface, not as the long-term ABI commitment.
+- Keep hints advisory and non-correctness-critical.
+
+Non-goals
+---------
+
+- No block-layer model is required for the first serious RFC.
+- No real migration or CXL backend is implemented here.
+- No tracepoints are added in this skeleton; observability is left to a later
+  RFC once the control-plane shape survives review.
+
+Design sketch
+-------------
+
+The proposed interface describes a virtual address range and a small operation
+set:
+
+- ``HBF_HINT_PREFETCH``
+- ``HBF_HINT_PROMOTE``
+- ``HBF_HINT_DEMOTE``
+- ``HBF_HINT_RELEASE``
+
+``HBF_HINT_PIN`` is intentionally omitted from v1. If a pinning concept is ever
+needed, it should likely be privileged and justified separately.
+
+The kernel-side helper validates the range and currently returns
+``-EOPNOTSUPP`` after basic checks. Future work may connect this to:
+
+- ``mm/migrate.c``
+- ``mm/memory-tiers.c``
+- ``mm/mempolicy.c``
+- ``drivers/cxl/core/``
+- ``drivers/cxl/mem.c``
+- ``drivers/cxl/region.c``
+- ``drivers/dax/kmem.c``
+
+This RFC skeleton exists only to make the memory-tier hint shape concrete.
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/hbf.h b/include/uapi/linux/hbf.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e0319e3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/hbf.h
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note */
+#ifndef _UAPI_LINUX_HBF_H
+#define _UAPI_LINUX_HBF_H
+
+#include <linux/ioctl.h>
+#include <linux/types.h>
+
+#define HBF_UAPI_VERSION	1
+#define HBF_IOCTL_MAGIC		'H'
+
+enum hbf_hint_op {
+	HBF_HINT_PREFETCH	= 1,
+	HBF_HINT_PROMOTE	= 2,
+	HBF_HINT_DEMOTE		= 3,
+	HBF_HINT_RELEASE	= 4,
+	/* HBF_HINT_PIN intentionally omitted from v1. */
+};
+
+struct hbf_hint_range {
+	__u32 version;
+	__u32 op;
+	__u64 flags;
+	__u64 start;
+	__u64 len;
+	__s32 target_nid;
+	__u32 reserved0;
+	__u64 deadline_ns;
+	__u64 user_tag;
+	__u64 reserved[6];
+};
+
+#define HBF_IOC_HINT	_IOW(HBF_IOCTL_MAGIC, 0x01, struct hbf_hint_range)
+
+#endif /* _UAPI_LINUX_HBF_H */
\ No newline at end of file
